From b940ab1f46f478395cdacb949b55f220f737a005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:48:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: migrate SDL 1.2 -> SDL3 API surface

Passage's entire SDL surface is small (raw video/input/audio, no
mixer/image/font libs), so this is one patch covering the full
migration rather than the multi-patch mechanical-rename series
doskutsu's much larger NXEngine-evo migration needed:

- Video: SDL_SetVideoMode -> SDL_CreateWindow + SDL_GetWindowSurface.
  SDL_Flip/SDL_UpdateRect -> SDL_UpdateWindowSurface (SDL3 dropped the
  hardware-double-buffer flag; SDL_DOUBLEBUF was requested
  unconditionally in the original, so the partial/full SDL_UpdateRect
  branches it gated were already dead code -- collapsed to one present
  call). SDL_FillRect -> SDL_FillSurfaceRect. Force fullscreen-only on
  DOS (__DJGPP__) -- no windowed VGA/VESA concept exists.
- Input: SDL_GetKeyState (indexed by keycode in SDL1.2) ->
  SDL_GetKeyboardState (indexed by SDL_Scancode in SDL3) -- all
  getKeyDown() call sites converted from SDLK_* to SDL_SCANCODE_*.
  event.key.keysym.sym -> event.key.key; SDL_KEYDOWN/SDL_QUIT ->
  SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN/SDL_EVENT_QUIT; lowercase single-letter keycodes
  (SDLK_q etc.) -> uppercase (SDLK_Q) per SDL3's renamed constants.
- Joystick: sequential-index SDL_JoystickOpen(0)/SDL_NumJoysticks ->
  instance-ID SDL_GetJoysticks()/SDL_OpenJoystick(id). Added a NULL
  guard around SDL_GetNumJoystickHats that the original called
  unconditionally even after a failed open -- a latent bug harmless
  under SDL1.2 but not worth carrying forward.
- Audio: SDL_OpenAudio(spec+callback)/SDL_CloseAudio ->
  SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream(devid, spec, callback,
  userdata)/SDL_DestroyAudioStream. The callback changed from a "push"
  model (write into a buffer SDL owns) to a "pull" model (SDL asks for
  N more bytes; supply them via SDL_PutAudioStreamData) -- musicPlayer's
  synth logic itself (Timbre/Envelope/note-grid stepping) is unchanged,
  only the buffer handoff at the end of audioCallback. SDL_LockAudio/
  SDL_UnlockAudio -> SDL_LockAudioStream/SDL_UnlockAudioStream against
  the new module-level audioStream handle.
- SDL_HINT_DOS_ALLOW_DIRECT_FRAMEBUFFER=1 set before SDL_Init on DOS --
  without it SDL3-DOS's window-surface flush silently writes nowhere
  visible (see <SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h>).
- g_pixtone_active_count: the shared SDL3-DOS Sound Blaster backend
  declares this as an "engine -> SDL extern" for a doskutsu/Cave-Story-
  specific Pixtone diagnostic (see sdl-dos-ports' shared/patches/
  sdl3-dos/README.md's "Known naming debt"). Passage has no Pixtone
  equivalent; defined here permanently at 0.

blowUp.cpp needed no changes: SDL_Surface's pixels/pitch/w/h fields are
unchanged between SDL1.2 and SDL3, and blowupOntoScreen() only touches
those.

Real-hardware-equivalent validation (2026-08-26): builds clean under
DJGPP, boots to title screen and into gameplay under DOSBox-X
(build/stage, dosbox-x-fast.conf, lfn=true pending the 8.3-rename
follow-up noted in PLAN.md) -- title screen and gameplay both render
and respond to keyboard input correctly. TITLE_SCREEN and PLAYABLE
milestones reached on the first successful compile.
